# UI terminology

The user is learning official UI names. When they use vague language, **do the work they asked for**, then **correct the term in the reply** (one short mapping, not a lecture). Use Apple HIG / SwiftUI words in follow-ups.

## Glossary (vague → official)

| They say | Official term |
|---|---|
| main menu, side panel, side bar | **sidebar** (`NavigationSplitView` sidebar column) |
| Mac / Devices / App labels | **section headers**; rows under them are **sidebar items** |
| bigger/smaller fonts for hierarchy | **typographic hierarchy** (title, headline, body, caption) |
| card | **card** (grouped surface); a row inside it is still a **list row** unless it is a **tile** |
| tile vs line | **tile** (grid cell, icon + title); **list row** (full-width horizontal item) |
| sub text under a name | **subtitle** / **secondary label** / **caption** |
| group by type vs brand | **sections** grouped by **category** |
| BLE / Bolt switcher thingy | **segmented control** (`Picker` + `.segmented`) |
| Add Device panel / popup | **sheet** (modal); the window is the **sheet**, not a panel |
| bottom bar next to Done | **footer**; Done is the **dismiss** action; a control to the left is a **leading** action |
| Past devices | **disconnected** (not “history”) |
| abrupt switch / jump | **layout jump**; if the window resizes, **intrinsic content size** changed. Prefer a **stable frame** + **content transition** (crossfade / slide) |
| animation for size | **frame animation**; sheets should usually **keep one size** and animate **content**, not the window |

Do not invent cute labels. Prefer HIG names in code comments and user-facing copy only when the UI already uses them.
